+ *   management (8-byte packets, 64), gdb R4 and gdb M4 (4-byte packets, 512 each), mxlog (to AP only, 4-byte, 4096).
+ *   Interrupt bits in the order Linux allocates them (to-host bits count up from 0; from-host R4/M4 from 1, bit 0
